<title>FRANCE: Alcatel, Total, Elf shares busy in block trades.</title>
<headline>Alcatel, Total, Elf shares busy in block trades.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Big blocks of Elf Aquitaine, Total, Alcatel Alsthom and Rhone-Poulenc shares changed hands in morning trade on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>One block of 3.18 million Total shares, or 1.3 percent of the group's capital traded at 557 francs at 0916 GMT, the SBF stock market authority confirmed.</p>
<p>At 0916 GMT a block of 2.1 million shares in Elf, or 0.7 percent of the company's capital, traded at 631 francs and a block of 1.55 million shares in Rhone-Poulenc or 0.4 percent of capital traded at 201.5 francs, it also said.</p>
<p>A block of 724,000 shares in Alcatel traded at 696 francs at 0848 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
